    The grid contains one or more connected components of non‑zero cells.
    Each component has exactly one cell with value 2; this cell lies on one of
    the component's border sides. The component is extended away from the
    component in the direction indicated by that side:

        • the side is determined by the position of the 2 inside the
          component's bounding box (top, bottom, left or right)
        • a line of 2's is drawn from the 2 to the grid border in that
          direction
        • for every step away from the original 2 (the “thickness” of the
          component in the direction of the line) we also fill the
          orthogonal neighbours with 3's

    The thickness equals (size of the component in the line direction) – 1.
    """
    if not grid:
        return grid

    n = len(grid)
    m = len(grid[0])

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # 1. find connected components (4‑connected) of non‑zero cells
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    visited = [[False] * m for _ in range(n)]
    components = []                      # list of (list of cells, bounding box, 2‑position)

    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(m):
            if grid[i][j] != 0 and not visited[i][j]]:
                # BFS/DFS to collect the component
                stack = [(i, j)]
                visited[i][j] = True
